  "answer": "The storefront is dropping specials that have an end date. I\u2019ll follow the debugging skill and trace how those dates are applied before changing anything.The admin product mapper stores the special end date on the start-date field, and the price calculator then requires the start date to be both before and after today. I\u2019ll add tests for those two cases first.The both-dates case fails because the discount check asks whether the start date is after today after already requiring it to be before today. End-date-only pricing works when the end date is stored on the right field, so next I\u2019ll confirm the admin mapper and then fix both.Special prices that include an end date never reached the storefront as a discount. The admin product mapper wrote that end date into the start-date field, and the price calculator then required the start date to be both before and after today. The mapper now stores the end date on the end-date field, and the calculator applies the special while the end date is still in the future.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialPriceTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"full Maven suite and live admin/storefront API\"], \"missing\": [\"a documented way to run integration tests without a local database\"]}",
